  {
   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "What research and trials exist?",
   "text": "There is a recruiting Phase 3 trial of a gene therapy called SGT-003, run by Solid Biosciences Inc., with study sites in Australia, Canada, and the United States [E5151ec3, Ed976d5e, Eba199a2, E22e9a82, E9ce3e84]. There is a recruiting Phase 3 trial of AOC 1044, run by Avidity Biosciences, Inc., with sites in Belgium, Germany, Spain, France, the United Kingdom, Italy, and the Netherlands [E5da2d1b, Ecb36749, E858b473, E8def594, Ecea297d, E014760e, E033d543]. There is a recruiting Phase 2 trial of KER-065, run by Keros Therapeutics, Inc., with a site in New Zealand [E4a681ba, Ecad00ee, E13e9f9e]. There is a recruiting Phase 2 and 3 trial of GNT0004, run by Genethon, with sites in Belgium, Spain, France, and the United Kingdom [E807d05a, E7658ee0, E37a6ead, Ed2a2e22, Ecb1e887, E1f2f606]. There is a Phase 2 trial of SAT-3247, run by Satellos Bioscience, Inc., that is active but no longer recruiting, with sites across several countries including the United States, Australia, Belgium, and Canada [E57e4c6f, E37573dd, Ec6f839a, E2f6f9e7, E7249c1f, E3c9b004]. Several United States government funders, NIH NIAID, NIH NIAMS, NIH NICHD, and NIH NIGMS, fund research grants connected to Duchenne [E7836040, Efa65347, E4217983, E30518c6, E35dc4a7, Eea693c5, E1437d1d, E04f2fe2]. Researchers named in these grants include Andreia Nunes [Eebac42f, E04f2fe2], Dongsheng Duan and Roland W. Herzog on the same grant [E7e30b9e, Ec404bc0, Efa65347], Douglas Paul Millay [E2fa7647, E30518c6], and Kurt Derek Christensen [E95361ab, Eea693c5].",
